{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.MarkovCosetLift","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovCosetLift","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductiveCyclicity"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.ce_trace_cosetSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.ce_trace_cosetSum","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovCosetLift.lean#L156-L179","doc":"**The linear lift — `hCE` for a coset-decomposed `x`.**\n\n`ce_trace_mid` gives `tr(a·(b·f·c)) = z·tr(a·(b·c))` on one mid coset. Summing,\n`tr(a·x) = tr(a·(E x))` for `x = a' + Σᵢ bᵢ·f·cᵢ` and `E x = a' + Σᵢ z • (bᵢ·cᵢ)`:\nboth sides reduce to `tr(a·a') + Σᵢ z·tr(a·(bᵢ·cᵢ))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.gwg_trace_cosetSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.gwg_trace_cosetSum","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovCosetLift.lean#L118-L154","doc":"**The linear lift — `hgwg` for a coset-decomposed `w`.**\n\nGiven the traced `g·w·g` reduction on the lower term `a` and on each mid term\n`bᵢ·f·cᵢ`, linearity of `tr` assembles it for `w = a + Σᵢ bᵢ·f·cᵢ` with\n`E w = a + Σᵢ z • (bᵢ·cᵢ)`.\n\nThis is the step `MarkovInductiveCyclicity`'s header names as the only one not\nmechanised. Its hypotheses are supplied by `gwg_trace_lower_shape` and\n`gwg_trace_mid_shape` above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.gwg_trace_mid_shape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.gwg_trace_mid_shape","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovCosetLift.lean#L87-L110","doc":"**Mid coset, normalised into the `E`-shape.** `gwg_trace_mid` produces\n`z·tr(x·b·f·f·c·y)`; the Hecke relation `f² = 1 + h̄·f` splits it as\n`tr(x·(z • (b·c))·y) + z·h̄·tr(x·(b·f·c)·y)` — the `hgwg` shape with\n`E(b·f·c) = z • (b·c)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.gwg_trace_lower_shape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.gwg_trace_lower_shape","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovCosetLift.lean#L69-L85","doc":"**Lower coset, normalised into the `E`-shape.** `gwg_trace_lower` produces\n`tr(x·a·y) + z·tr(x·a·hh·y)`; with the Hecke element `hh` being the scalar\n`h̄` (i.e. `hh = h̄ • 1`), the second term is `z·h̄·tr(x·a·y)`, which is the\n`hgwg` shape with `E a = a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.tr_finset_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.tr_finset_sum","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovCosetLift.lean#L51-L63","doc":"`tr` is additive over a `Finset` sum, from binary additivity plus `tr 0 = 0`.\n\nStated for a bare additive `tr : A → R` rather than a bundled `AddMonoidHom`,\nto match the interface style the rest of this development uses: the trace\narrives as a function with hypotheses, not as a structure. ","signatureChunk":0}]}